# Fin flutter: the Analyze view (speed against flutter speed over the flight, the shaded gap, the minimum and its margin) and the
# inspector's flutter chip and stiffness rows, for the example rocket and for thin balsa fins that fail.
# Run with the example rocket loaded: `cargo run -q -p bowshock -- drive --example crates/bowshock/scripts/flutter.drive out/flutter`
viewport 1280x1100
scale 1
# The example's linked fin set, picked in the Aero lane: the stiffness rows of 03 Material & finish and the flutter chip of 04.
click (922, 924)
screenshot inspector-example.png
click "Analyze"
click "Fin flutter"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot analyze-example.png
click "Build"
# Thin balsa fins: 1 mm thick, and the material swapped for balsa.
click (1180, 372)
type "1"
type enter
click "Birch plywood · 630 kg/m³"
click "Balsa · 170 kg/m³"
screenshot inspector-balsa.png
click "Analyze"
click "Fin flutter"
move (100, 1000)
move (102, 1002)
screenshot analyze-balsa.png
